Package: a-nas-docker-policy
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: A-NAS <zhongwater123@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: python3, systemd, iproute2
Description: require the site's address pool before Docker starts
 Docker's service and socket refuse to start until daemon.json supplies
 both bip and default-address-pools (docs/adr/0013). This host policy has
 its own package so rolling the product and a-nas-host back to a version
 from before the policy existed leaves the protection installed, just as
 it leaves Docker installed. It never starts or enables Docker.
